Experiment-2.1
Search Insert Position(leetcode-35)

Aim-Given a sorted array of distinct integers and a target value, return the index if the target is found. If not, return the index where it would be if it were inserted in order.
You must write an algorithm with O(log n) runtime complexity.

Algorithm-
1)Start.
2)Set left = 0 and right = n - 1.
3)While left <= right:
  >Compute mid = left + (right - left) / 2.
  >If nums[mid] == target, return mid.
  >Else if target > nums[mid], set left = mid + 1.
  >Else, set right = mid - 1.
4)Return left as the insertion index.
5)Stop.

Code-
class Solution {
public:
    int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
       int left=0;
       int right=nums.size()-1;

       while(left<=right){
        int mid=left+(right-left)/2;
        if(nums[mid]==target){
            return mid;
        }
        else if(target>nums[mid]){
            left=mid+1;
        }
        else{
            right=mid-1;
        }
       } 
       return left;
    }
};


Experiment-2.2
Implement Queue using Stacks(leetcode-232)

Aim-Implement a first in first out (FIFO) queue using only two stacks. The implemented queue should support all the functions of a normal queue (push, peek, pop, and empty).

Algorithm-
Push(x)
1)Start.
2)Move all elements from s1 to s2.
3)Push x into s1.
4)Move all elements from s2 back to s1.
5)Stop.
Pop()
1)Start.
2)Store the top element of s1.
3)Remove the top element from s1.
4)Return the stored element.
5)Stop.
Peek()
1)Start.
2)Return the top element of s1.
3)Stop.
Empty()
1)Start.
2)If s1 is empty, return true.
3)Otherwise, return false.
4)Stop.

Code-
class MyQueue {
public:
        stack<int>s1;
        stack<int>s2;
    MyQueue() {
        
    }
    
    void push(int x) {
        //s1->s2
        while(!s1.empty()){
            s2.push(s1.top());
            s1.pop();
        }
        //x->s1
        s1.push(x);
        //s2->s1
        while(!s2.empty()){
            s1.push(s2.top());
            s2.pop();
        }
    }
    
    int pop() {
        int x=s1.top();
        s1.pop();
        return x;
    }
    
    int peek() {
        return s1.top();
    }
    
    bool empty() {
        return s1.empty();
    }
};
